00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:38.340
Canadian TFSA holders holding AI-related names face immediate downside pressure

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.800
after Tokyo's Nikkei dropped more than 4% on chipmaker selling,

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.200
highlighting the need to size positions against sector rotation risk.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:54.200
The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,534, down 0.5%.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:01:01.120
The NASDAQ composite closed at 25,882, down 1.5%.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:08.300
The TSX composite closed at 35,340, down 0.2%.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:14.540
Heavy selling in AI and semiconductor names drove the broad decline with ripple effects visible

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:20.520
across Asian indices. The Bank of Canada's next scheduled interest rate announcement sits on

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.100
December 9, with markets currently pricing steady policy through year end.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.120
Earning season remains active for financials and industrials,

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.800
where results are producing clearer rotation signals than the tech heavy NASDAQ.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:42.180
Our simulated portfolio shows a cumulative profit of $266.87 across 42 trades.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:49.980
The matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ stands at plus 6.6% across 37 benchmark trades.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:57.200
Are we beating the NASDAQ this week? The most recent trade delivered plus 0.09% matched

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:03.060
window alpha, while the index fell 1.5%. While the broad market rotates,

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.600
one sector is quietly attracting policy-driven capital.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.120
Sector rotation into defense and industrial names is gaining traction as European

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:17.880
government's increased procurement spending. SAB's second quarter results beat expectations

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:23.520
on both sales and orders, demonstrating how rising defense budgets can create sustained

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:29.620
backlog visibility for contractors. Investors can implement this by screening for companies with

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:37.160
order backlog growth above 15% year over year, and defense revenue exposure above 40%.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:41.840
Then confirm the setup with a same-day volume check against the 20-day average.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.820
The approach has historically delivered excess returns during multi-year rearmament cycles,

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:53.020
but carries elevated geopolitical premium risk if budgets are later cut.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:59.660
Pairing the screen with a stop-loss 8% below entry limits draw down exposure during volatility

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:06.080
spikes. This setup is distinct from pure momentum entries because the catalyst is policy-driven

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:12.080
rather than earnings-surprise-driven. To act on these rotations, you need the right brokerage.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:19.160
Imagine you want to buy 200 shares of an industrial name trading on both the TSX and NYSE

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:25.300
right after the open. Your order fills at the ask on wealth-simple trade, but you notice the same

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:31.920
order would have cost an extra $4.95 on quest trade because the US leg triggered a commission.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:37.420
Wealth-simple trade offers commission-free trades inside registered accounts, but limits

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:46.900
advanced order types and has no margin capability. Quest trade charges $4.95 to $9.95 per trade,

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:52.000
yet provides free ETF purchases and solid mobile charting for active investors.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:04:01.080
Interactive brokers post the lowest margin rates, currently around 5.8% for CAD balances over $100,000,

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:09.140
and full access to 150-plus global exchanges. Bank-owned platforms such as TD Direct Investing and

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:15.860
RBC Direct integrate seamlessly with checking accounts yet carry higher commissions of $6.95

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:24.520
to $9.95 and slower execution on US names. The biggest mistake retail investors make is choosing a

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:29.620
brokerage solely on advertised commission rates without checking whether it supports the exact

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:36.200
markets and order types their strategy requires. Instead, match the platform to your account type

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:44.200
and trade frequency. Wealth-simple works for simple TFSA or RESP buy and hold. Quest-trade suits

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:51.280
occasional ETF and stock trades. Interactive brokers become useful once you need international access

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:57.180
or margin. With platforms sorted, let's see how our own practice book performed this week.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:03.960
This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only. No real money is involved. No new position

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:10.140
was initiated today. No setup today meets the three-factor threshold required during the current cold

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:16.560
streak. We are watching EpiRock for a potential rebound only if it closes above its 50-day moving

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:23.480
average on volume exceeding the 20-day average. The current regime shows average matched window alpha

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:31.620
of negative 0.98% over the last 10 trades. Any new position requires explicit volume confirmation

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:37.720
to avoid further underperformance. Skipping a trade when factors are misaligned preserves capital

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:44.140
and forces discipline in a statistically weak regime. The explicit trigger I am waiting for is a

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:50.000
close above the 50-day moving average accompanied by volume 50% above the 20-day average.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.860
Next Monday's focus will remain on the industrial sector once a qualifying setup appears.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:02.480
Given the current cold streak, today's practice decision was to stay on the sidelines. Yesterday

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:08.860
we reviewed the DAL earning surprise entry on record revenue and margin resilience despite peak

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:18.780
fuel costs. The trade entered at $87.94 on the Friday open and exited at $86.70 on the Thursday

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:30.220
close. The result was a loss of 1.41% or $14.10 on a $1,000 position. The trade lost 1.41% while

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:39.420
the NASDAQ fell 1.5% over the same window, delivering plus 0.09% alpha. The earnings catalyst produced

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:45.860
only modest relative outperformance because fuel cost concerns persisted and broader market rotation

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:52.280
away from travel names accelerated midweek. The lesson is to require volume confirmation above the

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:58.800
20-day average before entering momentum trades on earnings beats. The data vault AI tokenization

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:04.940
platform allows investors to gain fractional exposure to edge data center capacity through tokenized

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:11.380
infrastructure assets on a blockchain ledger. This gives retail investors access to a previously

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:17.460
illiquid asset class with 24-7 settlement and lower minimums than traditional private placements.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:24.100
Active Canadian investors managing TFSA accounts can use it to add non-correlated infrastructure

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:30.660
exposure without needing a separate private equity vehicle. Access is currently through the company's

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:37.040
direct token offering portal. Interactive brokers built in margin calculator lets users model borrowing

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:44.040
costs across CAD, USD, and Euro balances in real time before placing a leverage position.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:50.720
The tool surfaces the exact interest accrual for a proposed trade size, helping investors avoid

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:58.020
surprise margin calls during volatile sessions. It is most useful for accounts over $25,000 that

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:04.680
already qualify for portfolio margin. While we wait for better setups, two new tools can help active

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:11.300
investors. A deco hit a four-month high after BNP Perrybaugh upgraded the stock to outperform.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:18.280
Staffing giant a deco rallied after the upgrade, showing that labor market data can still drive single

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:26.300
name moves even when broader indices fall. Add ADE on the SWX exchange to the industrial's watchlist

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:30.420
and wait for a close above the July 10th high before considering entry.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:37.260
Truest financial posted inline earnings but missed revenue estimates. Truest's results illustrate

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:43.400
how net interest margin pressure continues to weigh on regional banks. Hold existing US bank

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:49.040
exposure and do not add until the next rate decision window clarifies margin trajectories.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:56.280
42% of Canadians say an unexpected expense could derail their finances according to an RBC poll.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:02.920
Nearly 4 in 10 lower income households lack any emergency fund, underscoring the priority

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:10.180
of liquidity buffers before increasing equity risk. Direct any new TFSA contributions into a high

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:17.200
interest cash ETF until the emergency fund target equals three months of expenses. South Africa

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:24.100
eyes $46 billion for industrial hubs by April. The planned investment push targets manufacturing

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:29.480
revival and could create new listed vehicle exposure for emerging market industrials.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:36.920
Add the eye shares MSCI South Africa ETF to the monthly review list but size any position below

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:43.520
2% until infrastructure project milestones are confirmed. A few quick hits worth adding to the watch

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:52.440
list. Our simulated portfolio across 42 trades shows a win rate of 55% with 23 wins 18 losses and

00:09:52.440 --> 00:10:03.360
one break even. Cumulative profit stands at $266.87. Average return per trade is plus 0.64%.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:11.280
The best trade returned plus 20.11%. And the worst return negative 11.80%.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:17.960
The current streak is two losses. Our AI analysis is learning from volume patterns and adjusting

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:24.580
entry filters accordingly. Now here's something that most retail investors get wrong. Leg triggered

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:31.680
a commission. Quest trades suits occasional ETF and stock trades. Before we wrap, open your brokerage

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:37.660
platform, pull up the order book for any US listed industrial stock you own and note the current bid

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:44.060
ask spread in sense. Compare it to the 20 day average spread shown in the platform's analytics tab.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:50.680
If today's spread is more than 50% wider than the average, reduce your next plan purchase size by

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:56.960
half to account for higher transaction costs. I've got my eye on volume confirmation signals in

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:02.900
the industrial sector for Monday's watch list. That wraps up today's modern investing techniques.

